            <ArticleTitle>Bathing Trunk Inevus Associated with Neurofibromatosis and Raised Intracranial Tension.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>106-107</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 17-year-old boy had bathing trunk nevus with multiple large neurofibromata on the nevus and raised intracranial tension presenting with bilateral papilloedema and pyramidal tract sings. This combination, of features is extremely rare.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
